## F: English against the Arabic (separate pass), 2026-11-14

Batch 1 (1 to 15). Findings, each fixed:

- 02: "may Allah be pleased with him, also" read awkwardly and misplaced أيضا; now "It is also narrated from Umar".
- 04: "commanded to write four things" dropped بأربع كلمات ("with four words"); now "commanded with four words: to write …".
- 06: "grazing his flock": "his flock" is not in the Arabic; now in square brackets.
- Checked and kept: 01 "whoever's emigration was" (كانت past, kept as past); 04 كتاب rendered "what was written", not "the Book", since it is the decree written for him; 10 the two ayahs translated plainly inside quotation marks, no commentary; 11 ريحانته kept literal ("his sweet basil"); 14 الثيب الزاني rendered "the married person who commits adultery" (الثيب covers man and woman).

