## Independent verification, 2026-11-15

A fresh agent that wrote none of the content checked hadith 1 to 15. Nothing here is
scholar-reviewed.

- **Arabic**: every witness page was fetched again into an empty cache and `collate.mjs --vowels`
  re-run. Its output is the same as the block above, line for line, and every stored
  `skeletonSha256` matches. Each matn was also read by eye on Ibn Daqiq al-'Id's page, with
  al-Nawawi's attribution line; hadith 2, 4, 11 and 12 were read on al-Haytami's vowelled page
  too. The readings chosen where the prints differ are as the provenance notes say. Each item
  has at least one printed (non-Sunnah.com) witness that agrees with ours; in 4, 9 and 10 no
  print is letter-identical, and the notes name each difference (a word-join in Ibn Daqiq for 4
  and 9; in 10 Ibn Daqiq's print drops two phrases that al-Haytami and hadith-api both have).
- **English**: re-read sentence by sentence against the Arabic. One change: 11, ريحانته is now
  "his fragrant flower" (rev 3). "Sweet basil" named one species; ريحانة is any sweet-smelling
  plant, and al-Haytami glosses it "ريحان طيب الرائحة". No omission, addition or softening found
  elsewhere.
- **Citations**: every Bukhari, Muslim, Tirmidhi, Nasa'i and Ibn Majah number was found in the
  Dar al-Minhaj editors' footnotes (Ibn Majah 3976 on p. 301); 11 and 12 also in the footnotes
  of Ibn Rajab's editors (1/278, 1/287).
- **Gradings**: 11, al-Tirmidhi's "وهذا حديث حسن صحيح" read after no. 2518, and al-Nawawi quotes
  it; Ibn Rajab: "وصححه الترمذي". 12, al-Nawawi's "حديث حسن" read in both prints; al-Tirmidhi's
  word after no. 2317 is "غريب"; Ibn Rajab's quoted sentence read at 1/287, with Ahmad, Ibn
  Ma'in, al-Bukhari and al-Daraqutni named for the mursal view. The note on 12 now also gives
  Ibn Abd al-Barr's view from the same passage, which supports al-Nawawi, so both sides are
  shown (rev 2).
- **Notes**: each note's paraphrase was read against the page it cites; all fifteen hold.
- Nothing was removed. `build-deen --check` green (the G8 warning on 11 is the name al-Hasan).

